// =============================================================================
// core/hash/mod.vr — hash functions, grouped by the guarantee they give
// =============================================================================
// Layer: 1 (depends on core primitives only)
// =============================================================================
//

// A hash function is chosen by the property the caller needs, and the
// four properties below are NOT interchangeable. This module is split
// by guarantee — not by algorithm family, not by era — so that the
// mount line at a call site already states what the caller is relying
// on, and a wrong choice is visible in review without opening the file.
//

//  * `checksum` — detects accidental corruption. NOT collision
//                 resistant, NOT keyed. An adversary can construct
//                 collisions trivially. Use for wire/storage integrity
//                 against noise, never against an attacker.
//
//  * `fast`     — fast, well-distributed, NON-cryptographic. Use for
//                 hash tables, sketches, sharding, cache keys. An
//                 adversary who controls inputs can force collisions
//                 (algorithmic-complexity attacks) — key such uses
//                 with `core.mac.hmac` instead.
//
//  * `crypto`   — collision- and preimage-resistant. Use for content
//                 addressing, commitments, signatures, key schedules.
//
//  * `legacy`   — cryptographic by design, BROKEN in practice, kept
//                 only because a wire protocol mandates the exact
//                 bytes. Never a free choice.
//
// Keyed authentication is not a hash: see `core.mac`.
//

// Placement rule: a module belongs here iff it maps bytes to a
// fixed-size digest using core primitives alone. Anything that needs
// a key, a policy, an identity, or a certificate belongs above —
// `core.mac` or `core.security` respectively. This module MUST NOT
// grow a dependency on either.
//

// =============================================================================

module core.hash;

public module checksum;
public module fast;
public module crypto;
public module legacy;
